# SAP extraction cron jobs - install with:  sudo -u sapapp crontab -e
# Times are in the server's timezone (EC2 default: UTC). 00:30 UTC = 06:00 IST.
# Exit codes: 0 ok, 1 failed, 2 partial, 75 skipped (previous run still running).
# Detailed log: /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.log ; JSON result of each run: log/cron.out
#
# BSID / BSAD do NOT need cron: the systemd worker (deploy/sap-extraction-worker.service)
# polls SAP every 60 s and sends new / changed rows to the ingestion API (queue).

# Customer master KNA1 -> active_kna1, every hour. The worker reads the customer name of each VBRK
# invoice from it (customer_name_vbrk = kunrg -> sendername). A customer created in SAP has no name
# on its invoices until this ran. Does not touch active_bt3h (bt3h sync runs only after a BSID extract).
5 * * * * /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh sync --tables KNA1 >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1

# Optional - full loads of the other non-delta [sap] tables (e.g. T001) once a day at 06:00 IST.
# Not needed while [sap] tables only lists delta tables and KNA1.
# 30 0 * * * /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh sync >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1

# Fallback only - without the systemd worker: one delta poll + ingestion cycle every minute.
# A cycle that finds an ingestion still running just polls and leaves ingestion alone.
# * * * * * /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh delta >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1

# Fallback only - direct copy active_bsid -> active_bt3h while the ingestion API is not available.
# Remove it once the worker ingests BSID, otherwise invoices appear twice in active_bt3h (AR Inbox);
# then run deploy/sql/migrate_ar_inbox_20261121.sql to remove the IT_Invoice rows it wrote.
# */5 * * * * /opt/sap-extraction-api/deploy/run_cron.sh sync-bt3i >> /opt/sap-extraction-api/log/cron.out 2>&1
